  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-24T20:57:42.895Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If your world has more than 32 sounds, some will be culled (Unity limitation?)\n\nThe problem is that it seems to cull player voices first rather than world sounds, leading to frustrating situations where you can't talk to each other.\n\nThe other problem is that sounds that are completely silent due to being out of range still take up a slot, and are prioritized over player voices.\n\nI've created a test world at wrld_f03e1817-174a-4d9f-8a19-746d6eae1c2e\nclick the boxes to activate sounds. The red bars on top of the toggled boxes indicate how many audio sources are enabled. Range of the audio sources is 1 meter.\n\nThe green trigger contains audio sources that are set to Loop Disabled, which works as expected (no longer takes up a sound slot after finishing playing)\n\nThe red trigger has the audio source script disabled, also works as expected, no sound slot taken.\n\nExpected behaviour: Player voices are always prioritized over world sounds. Higher concurrent sound limit.",
